<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AssemblyName>Com.H.Data.Common</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Com.H.Data.Common</RootNamespace>
    <Version>10.1.0.10</Version>
    <Authors>Hussein Al Bayati</Authors>
    <Description>Run SQL on any ADO.NET connection and get the rows back as strongly typed objects (ExecuteQuery&lt;T&gt;, ExecuteQueryAsync&lt;T&gt;) or as dynamic objects (ExecuteQuery, ExecuteQueryAsync), streamed as IEnumerable&lt;T&gt; or IAsyncEnumerable&lt;T&gt;. The methods extend DbConnection and DbCommand; ExecuteCommand and ExecuteCommandAsync run statements that return no rows. Parameters are written as {{name}} in the SQL and always sent as real database parameters, never concatenated into it. Their values come from an anonymous object, a dictionary, a JsonElement or JSON text, and the delimiters can be changed. Typed results map columns to properties by name, or by [DataMember] or [JsonPropertyName]. JSON and XML columns can be returned as nested objects. Works with SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL and MariaDB, SQLite, Oracle, DB2 and any other ADO.NET provider; on ODBC and OleDb the named parameters become positional ? parameters automatically. No package dependencies on .NET 8 and later. Targets .NET 10, 9 and 8, and .NET Standard 2.0, which includes .NET Framework 4.6.1 and later.</Description>
    <Copyright>Hussein Al Bayati</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/H7O/Com.H.Data.Common</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageIcon>128x128.jpg</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>nuget.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/H7O/Com.H.Data.Common</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>ado.net;sql;micro-orm;typed;dynamic;async;iasyncenumerable;parameterized-query;sql-server;postgresql;mysql;sqlite;oracle;db2;odbc;oledb;netstandard2.0</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Three fixes. 1) An error raised after the first result set (SQL Server THROW or RAISERROR after a SELECT, or a later statement that fails) is now thrown once the caller has read every row; closing the reader used to discard it. A caller that stops reading early still doesn't see it. Only the first result set is returned, as before. 2) A single column with no name (SQL Server COUNT(*) without an alias) returns one bare value per row (null for NULL, and default(T) for NULL in typed ExecuteQuery&lt;T&gt;); it used to return each row twice, and a NULL three times. 3) ExecuteCommand and ExecuteCommandAsync honour closeConnectionOnExit: they close the connection, without disposing it, also when the first statement fails. They also dispose the command they create.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    
    <!-- Deterministic builds for reproducibility -->
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    
    <!-- Source Link - enables stepping into source code when debugging -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    
    <!-- Embed debug symbols in the assembly (avoids separate .snupkg) -->
    <DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Source Link for GitHub -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="10.0.401" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Polyfill packages for netstandard2.0 (IAsyncEnumerable, IAsyncDisposable,
       EnumeratorCancellationAttribute, System.Text.Json, dynamic runtime binder) -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CSharp" Version="4.7.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\128x128.jpg">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>

    <None Include=".\nuget.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>


</Project>
